X:1
T:Bújj, bújj, zöld ág
T:Crawl Through, Green Branch
C:traditional (Hungary)
O:Hungary, Baranya county
R:children's game (arch game)
S:Kiss Áron, Magyar gyermekjáték-gyűjtemény (Budapest, 1891), Újhold-játék No. 4, p. 207
N:A Hungarian arch game, still one of the best known. Two children join hands and hold them high to make a gate; the others, holding hands in a line, pass under it while everyone sings. In this version from Baranya the line sings the first verse ("Let us through, bridge-master!") and the gatekeepers answer with the second ("I won't let you through!"); then all sing "Bújj, bújj", and "raj-ta" (through!) is sung once for each child passing under, as many as there are. The gate closes on the last child, who joins the gatekeepers, until all are caught (Kiss, pp. 206-207). Kiss's 1891 regional spellings are kept; today's school words run "Bújj, bújj, zöld ág, zöld levelecske". The translation and the tempo are ours.
Q:1/4=96
M:2/4
L:1/8
K:F
